# Gitignored files Claude Code copies into every worktree it creates
# (`--worktree`, subagent worktrees, desktop parallel sessions). .gitignore
# syntax; only files that match AND are gitignored are copied, so nothing
# tracked is duplicated.
#
# This is for state a worktree needs to have as its OWN files. State that
# belongs to the PROJECT rather than the branch is not copied — it is
# resolved to the main checkout at runtime via `settings.main_worktree`
# (lib/settings.py), so there is exactly one of it and it never drifts:
#
#   db/regin.db                  trace store
#   db/regin_memory.db           agent-memory store
#   .regin/memory/tree/          exported memory tree
#   config/settings.local.json   machine config (tokens, repo paths)
#
# Listing any of those here would create a second, diverging copy that the
# code would then ignore. Don't.

# The agent's own config: skills, subagents, slash commands, hook settings.
# A worktree without these silently loses every project skill. Enumerated per
# directory rather than as `.claude/` so `.claude/worktrees/` — the worktrees
# themselves — can never be copied into a worktree.
.claude/skills/**
.claude/agents/**
.claude/commands/**
.claude/settings.json

# Not copied on purpose:
#   .venv/                a worktree with its own venv becomes a second regin
#                         install; use the main checkout's interpreter
#   .claude/worktrees/    recursive
#   node_modules/         re-installable, large
